  "findings": [
    "Both reference and candidate already use the same unified Registration map and nested ConvertFn/BorrowedConversion layouts. Hot conversion lookup source is unchanged.",
    "The exact measured borrowed_wrong loop calls try_convert_for_property in both artifacts. Its warm miss outer function and Option<&BorrowedConversion>::cloned helper have the same executed instruction structure modulo addresses.",
    "The final candidate HashMap::get called by both borrowed and boxed public conversions retains an extra direct call to BuildHasherDefault<IdHasher>::hash_one. Reference inlines its rotate-left-32 plus xor. Candidate must also move/save/reload additional key registers.",
    "Pre-LTO reference hash_one is already two loads, rotate and xor. Candidate hash_one remains a stack hasher with two direct calls to IdHasher::write_u64. That method moved from CGU13 to CGU07 while hash_one remains in CGU13; it has no inline annotation.",
    "The candidate hash_one body simplifies during FatLTO to mov/rotate/xor/ret, but its outer call boundary remains in the final measured lookup. This executes even on an unregistered key, so it is a concrete common overhead candidate for the borrowed_wrong result.",
    "Destination ElementRef<Target>, nullable Ref<Target>, source bool and source Ref<Target> TypeId bytes are identical between binaries. This rules out changed identities for these measured keys, but is not a complete runtime map probe-count audit.",
    "A different shared Registration lookup/accessor routine in both binaries has identical inline hashing. That routine is not the lookup called by the measured public conversion functions; inspecting only it would miss the surviving hash_one call."
  ],
  "interpretation_limits": [
    "The observed extra call is causal instruction overhead, but its exact share of the measured timing regression has not been isolated by a paired fixed build.",
    "The fixture is held out of both PGO training workloads. Borrowed public conversion profile entries are zero in both reference and stage2; boxed entries remain257.",
    "Code layout, indirect target behavior, map occupancy and CPU effects can contribute separately. No precise percentage is attributed to the extra call before measurement.",
    "Exact hash_one profile records also differ:65774 versus115042, same CFG hash0x0a4d0ad3efffffff. Their difference49268 equals the nonempty lookup count represented in the main-CGU HashMap::get branch weights. This is consistent with early inlining changing which dynamic calls reach the separately instrumented hash_one body; do not treat its standalone counter as a direct workload comparison."
  ],
  "minimal_trial": {
    "change": "Add #[inline(always)] only to IdHasher::write_u64 so the body is available to hash_one before pre-LTO inlining. This is the demonstrated two-operation boundary; do not combine enum/accessor annotations in the first trial.",
    "public_api_change": false,
    "algorithm_or_map_change": false,
    "required_check": "Inspect candidate pre-LTO hash_one for disappearance of both write_u64 calls; inspect final measured lookup for no remaining hash_one call; then paired production-flag fixture and original correctness gate.",
    "patch": "/tmp/ferro496-conversion-recovery/inline-id-hash.patch"
  },
